  "created": "2026-09-05T00:58:42.16Z",
  "description": ".NET client library for InferHub — a self-hosted, Ollama-compatible LLM inference mesh. Typed requests over HTTP, dependency-injection friendly, small surface. Point it at a coordinator and call chat, generate (blocking + streaming), embeddings, the vector data-plane (upsert/query/retrieve), opt-in RAG retrieval (grounded chat/generate with source ids), model listing and status from C#. A second interface covers the OpenAI-compatible dialect (/v1/chat/completions, /v1/completions, /v1/embeddings, /v1/models) and the provider steer; a third covers audio — transcription, subtitles, and speech you can stream as it is synthesised; a fourth covers images — generations, edits and variations, plus an async job seam with per-step progress over SSE and read-once content; a fifth covers video in OpenAI's asynchronous Videos dialect, with a polled watch and read-once content; a sixth covers the document corpus — ingest text or a file, list documents, read their chunks, delete, and search a collection with vector, keyword or hybrid retrieval and optional reranking. The separate admin client covers fleet ops (list/cordon/drain/uncordon/deregister nodes), vector collection lifecycle (create/drop/rebuild) and the live admin event stream (SSE with reconnect).",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
